+
+# Technical Design
+
+## Context
+
+ledger-api runs on PostgreSQL 14 in three places: `docker-compose.yml`
+(`postgres:14`, named volume `pgdata` mounted at `/var/lib/postgresql/data`,
+holding each developer's data), CI (`postgres:14` service container), and
+production on Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL 14. The production database was created
+on PostgreSQL 11 in 2019 and upgraded in place to 14 in 2023. PostgreSQL 14
+reaches end of life in November 2026.
+
+## Decision
+
+Move all three environments to PostgreSQL 18, the newest major version, which
+RDS offers.
+
+- Local: the official image keeps its data under `/var/lib/postgresql` from
+  version 18 on (in a version-specific folder below it), so the new service
+  mounts a new volume `pgdata18` at `/var/lib/postgresql`. Data moves by dump
+  and restore: `make db-upgrade` runs `pg_dumpall` against the running 14
+  container to `backups/pre-18.sql`, starts `postgres:18` on `pgdata18`, and
+  restores the dump with `psql`. The old `pgdata` volume stays until the
+  developer has checked the restored data; then `docker volume rm` removes it.
+- CI: the service container becomes `postgres:18`.
+- Production: before the upgrade, check which roles still have MD5 passwords,
+  since roles from the PostgreSQL 11 era can, and PostgreSQL 18 deprecates MD5:
+  `SELECT * FROM rds_tools.role_password_encryption_type();` lists each role's
+  password type. Set `password_encryption = scram-sha-256` in the RDS parameter
+  group, reset the passwords of the roles the check lists, and run the check
+  again until none shows md5. Then take a manual RDS snapshot and upgrade with an RDS blue/green
+  deployment to 18. Rollback: until the switchover is confirmed, traffic can
+  switch back to the 14 environment; after it, restore the snapshot. The whole
+  sequence, rollback included, is rehearsed first on an instance restored from
+  a snapshot.
+
+## Acceptance Coverage
+
+- `AC-001`: local, CI, and production all run PostgreSQL 18.
+- `AC-002`: `make db-upgrade` moves each developer's data by dump and restore.
+- `AC-003`: blue/green with a snapshot, rehearsed with its rollback.
+
+## Build Plan
+
+1. Add the 18 service, the `pgdata18` volume, and `make db-upgrade`.
+2. Change the CI service image.
+3. Production runbook in `docs/operations.md`.
